    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d156">

                <pb facs="0219" n="137" xml:id="pg137"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 811.34537/56.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1911-04-17"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">April 17, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 758.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the project to enlarge
                    our naval station at Guantánamo, I have the honor to transmit herewith a copy of
                    a confidential memorandum which I read to Sr. Sanguily, the Cuban secretary of
                    state, this afternoon<anchor n="1" xml:id="d156-f1"/>.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.],</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John B. Jackson.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d156-a1.xml" xpointer="d156-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d156-f1" n="1" xml:id="d156-f1-content">
                <p>For remainder of this dispatch see Naval Station at Guantánamo, <ref
                        target="#pg121">p. 121</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
